WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:03.150
Notation in klavar

2
00:00:03.250 --> 00:00:09.850
Click Klavar: the lines are the black keys and time runs from top to bottom.

3
00:00:09.950 --> 00:00:17.850
Step input: switch on Step input and play the notes one by one; the cursor moves on by itself.

4
00:00:17.950 --> 00:00:23.750
Play a chord simply by pressing all its keys at once.

5
00:00:23.850 --> 00:00:31.083
Undo (Ctrl+Z) takes the input back step by step.

6
00:00:31.183 --> 00:00:45.583
Recording works the same: click Record and play. A red line follows along; held keys show in grey.

7
00:00:45.683 --> 00:00:52.517
Read from top to bottom: an open head is a white key, a solid head a black key.

8
00:00:52.617 --> 00:00:58.983
The stem points to the hand: right is the right hand, left is the left hand.

9
00:00:59.083 --> 00:01:03.283
The pedal sits on the narrow staff at the left.

10
00:01:03.383 --> 00:01:10.883
For each staff you choose the hand: automatic, R, L, Ped. or R+L with a split point.

11
00:01:10.983 --> 00:01:17.117
Is a note in the wrong hand? Select it and click ← L or R →.

12
00:01:17.217 --> 00:01:22.983
Save the klavar drawing as SVG, or print it via Print / PDF.

13
00:01:23.083 --> 00:01:27.917
Staff notation? See the video Notation on staves.
